   "notes": "Galactica is a decoder-only Transformer following Vaswani et al. with modifications (GeLU, learned positional embeddings, no biases, 2048 context, 50k BPE vocab). Five sizes are reported in the models table (125M, 1.3B, 6.7B, 30B, 120B); I set primary_config to GAL 120B since the title/abstract single it out as the headline, open-sourced model. All size fields come from that table except d_ff, which is not stated. Norm is LayerNorm but explicitly WITHOUT bias ('no biases in any ... layer norms'); the schema's 'layernorm' option assumes learned weight and bias, so this is an imperfect match (bias omitted). norm_placement (pre/post), norm_eps, rope fields, scale, tied embeddings, parallel_block, and MoE are not stated. Residual and causal attention are taken as inherited from the declared Transformer decoder-only architecture. Dropout p=0.1 is a training detail, not represented in the IR. The block_ops order shown is a standard decoder block; exact pre/post norm placement is not stated by the paper."
